<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 724–785</span> · Also known as Cauac Sky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat was the ruler of the Maya city of Quiriguá, installed in 724 under the authority of Copán. In 738 he captured and sacrificed Copán's king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waxaklajuun-ubaah-kawiil">Uaxaclajuun Ub'aah K'awiil</a>, freeing Quiriguá and taking control of trade on the Motagua river. He commissioned Quiriguá's giant carved stelae, the tallest in the Maya world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kak-tiliw-chan-yopaat.jpg" alt="K'ak' Tiliw Chan Yopaat" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blervis · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%CA%BCak%CA%BC_Tiliw_Chan_Yopaat_on_Stela_E.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
